## Communications
## Metal–Organic Frameworks
Beyond mixing: The proper combination of non-isostructural metal–organic frameworks in terms of solid solutions can drastically improve the porosity $(150\%)$ and optical $\mathsf{O}_{2}$ sensitivity (410 times) compared with the original phases. An oxygen-sensing MOF (MAF-2) can undergo structure changes and property improvements when its molecular building blocks are mixed and solid solutions are formed.
